  "question": {
    "text": "Remainder when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>64</mn><msup><mn>32</mn><mn>32</mn></msup></msup></math> is divided by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math> is equal to _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>64</mn><msup><mn>32</mn><mn>32</mn></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>63</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn><mtext>times</mtext></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mn>64</mn><msup><mn>32</mn><mn>32</mn></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>63</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>32</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Now we know that by binomial theorem,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>32</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mmultiscripts><mo>·</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mmultiscripts><mo>·</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mmultiscripts><mo>·</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>·</mo><msup><mn>63</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>32</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>α</mi></math></p><p>So, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>64</mn><msup><mn>32</mn><mn>32</mn></msup></msup></math> is divided by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math> we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> as remainder.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
